---
/**
 * Section 04 — three questions that arrive after a run, as things that
 * happened rather than as features.
 *
 * Each scenario leads in plain engineering English and the code or the output
 * follows it, never the other way round. The excerpts are short on purpose: a
 * reader who wants the whole log has /provenance/ one click away.
 */
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

/* weather/output.txt:9-15, trimmed to four of six rows. */
const weather = `  world          dT K   rho    IMU dep  onset s  dwell s   drift(dark) m     terminal m
  standard_day      0   1.00     1.00     13.1     55.7    41.60 +- 1.97   0.133 (max 0.195)
  hot_day          20   0.90     1.20     13.6     55.5    48.64 +- 2.40   0.141 (max 0.212)
  cold_day        -25   1.10     1.25     12.8     55.9    50.68 +- 2.93   0.132 (max 0.206)
  polar_winter    -40   1.20     1.40     12.4     56.1    58.71 +- 2.27   0.151 (max 0.219)`;

/* corridor/output.txt:56-62, verbatim. */
const blackout = `regime -> slip (GNSS-available), Kn=0.07829109848665225
nav: aided (position fix folded)
regime -> slip (GNSS-denied), Kn=0.012690837165407727
nav: dead reckoning (no usable fix)
march paused at step 131
!!ContextAlternation!!: world 'nominal_descent' replaced with 'fine_bank_08'`;

/* retropulsion/output.txt:13-40, the Act headers, condensed. */
const acts = `--- Act: BURN — supersonic retropulsion under the SRP envelope ---
  steps  731 | altitude    18.50 km | Mach  0.60 | rebuilds 0
  regime: continuum / subsonic / burn

--- Act: TERMINAL — cutoff, subsonic re-seed, touchdown ---
  steps 2516 | altitude     0.01 km | Mach  0.01 | rebuilds 1
  regime: continuum / subsonic / burn / touchdown`;
---
<section class="cfd-sec page" data-rise>
  <header class="sec-head">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-coord">
      <span class="ix">04 / 05</span><span class="lb">In practice</span>
    </p>
    <h2>Three questions that arrive after the run</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The case ran overnight, the result is on the screen, and the first thing
      the room asks is a what-if. These are the three shapes that question
      takes.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="panel corner-brackets body-panel rise">
    <h3>“What if it had been a hot day?”</h3>
    <p class="body">
      Six atmospheres, eight receiver-noise draws each, forty-eight descents,
      one gated table. The answer was not the expected one: the inertial unit
      does not behave as assumed in the cold. Polar-winter mean drift through
      blackout came out 58.71 m against a standard day's 41.60 m. The gate
      requires that separation to clear two combined standard deviations before
      it counts as a finding; it cleared 5.7. Four of the six rows are below,
      with the drift column on the right.
    </p>
    <Code code={weather} lang="text" themes={SHIKI} />

    <h3>“The link dropped — when did the filter go blind?”</h3>
    <p class="body">
      One append-only log carries flow, chemistry, navigation and control in a
      single sequence, so the answer is two adjacent lines rather than four logs
      correlated after the fact. In the excerpt below, the third line is the
      flow reporting the link gone and the fourth is the filter falling back to
      dead reckoning. Nothing scheduled that. The evolved electron density
      located it.
    </p>
    <Code code={blackout} lang="text" themes={SHIKI} />

    <h3>“It left the envelope — at which stage?”</h3>
    <p class="body">
      Each leg reports the classification it ended in, so a run that changed
      character can be named at the stage it did so. The two act headers below
      are consecutive: the vehicle is supersonic under burn in the first and
      subsonic at touchdown in the second, and the classifier counted eight such
      transitions across the descent.
    </p>
    <Code code={acts} lang="text" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p class="more">
      <a href="/provenance/">The full provenance record</a>
      <a href="/tutorial/">The three-walk tutorial</a>
      <a href="/examples/">Worked examples</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cfd-sec { max-width: var(--w-panel); }
  .sec-head { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .sec-head h2 { margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-3); }
  .lede { color: var(--fg-1); max-width: var(--measure-lede); margin: 0; }

  .body-panel { padding: var(--space-5); }
  .body { color: var(--fg-1); font-size: var(--t-body-sm); max-width: var(--measure); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); }

  .body-panel h3 {
    font-size: var(--t-h4);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-1);
  }
  .body-panel h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; border-top: none; }

  .more {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
  }
</style>
